# Plates & Progress — SaaS starter

Web app with accounts, synced data, and a paid Pro tier. Deploy time: ~30–45 min.

## 1. Supabase (accounts + database) — free tier is fine

1. Go to supabase.com → New project.
2. Project → SQL Editor → New query → paste the contents of `schema.sql` → Run.
3. Project → Settings → API → copy your **Project URL** and **anon public key**.
4. Open `index.html` and paste them into `SUPABASE_URL` and `SUPABASE_ANON_KEY` near the top of the `<script>` tag.
5. Settings → Authentication → make sure "Enable email confirmations" is on (default) or off if you want instant sign-in during testing.

## 2. Stripe (payments) — no code needed for the basic version

1. Go to dashboard.stripe.com → Products → add a product, e.g. "Pro" at $4.99/month (recurring).
2. Payment Links → create a link for that product.
3. Copy the link and paste it into `STRIPE_PAYMENT_LINK` in `index.html`.
4. Developers → Webhooks → Add endpoint. You'll fill in the URL after deploying (step 3 below) — it'll be `https://your-app.vercel.app/api/stripe-webhook`. Select the event `checkout.session.completed` (and `customer.subscription.deleted` if you want cancellations to revoke access).
5. Copy the **webhook signing secret** (starts with `whsec_`) and your **secret key** (starts with `sk_`) — you'll need both for step 3.

## 3. Deploy to Vercel (free tier is fine)

1. Push this folder to a GitHub repo.
2. Go to vercel.com → New Project → import the repo.
3. Under Environment Variables, add:
   - `STRIPE_SECRET_KEY` = your Stripe secret key
   - `STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET` = the webhook signing secret from step 2.4
   - `SUPABASE_URL` = same project URL as above
   - `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` = Supabase → Settings → API → **service_role** key (different from the anon key — keep this one secret, never put it in index.html)
4. Deploy. Vercel gives you a live URL like `https://your-app.vercel.app`.
5. Go back to Stripe's webhook setup and paste in the real URL: `https://your-app.vercel.app/api/stripe-webhook`.

## 4. Test it

1. Visit your Vercel URL, create an account, log a workout.
2. Click "Upgrade to Pro" — use Stripe's test card `4242 4242 4242 4242` if you're still in test mode.
3. Check your Supabase `profiles` table — `is_pro` should flip to `true` within a few seconds.

## What's already handled
- Per-user accounts and data isolation (Row Level Security in `schema.sql`)
- Free tier limited to last 5 sessions; Pro unlocks full history
- Stripe → Supabase sync via the webhook, so Pro unlocks automatically after payment

## What you'll likely want to add next
- Password reset flow (Supabase supports this out of the box, just needs a UI)
- A real progress chart on the synced version (the local-only version I built earlier has one — port it over)
- Terms of service / privacy policy page (Stripe requires a working link to these before you can go live)
- Move Stripe out of test mode when ready to charge real cards
